From 6e3d82c85423fc5bbf3a3f487a012e6560928a62 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: thibaut <thibaut-leaux-angeli@live.fr>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 16:33:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 26/33] d3d12: OpenExistingHeapFromAddress backs a heap with
 the caller's memory (VK_EXT_external_memory_host)

The retail executable opens the 64 KiB graphics region it has just committed with XMemVirtualAlloc
through device slot 48 right after its first queue and fence; the layer answered E_NOTIMPL and the
title asserted.

The call now answers as the host runtime does on an RTX 4090 and WARP (six cases measured in
d3d12_existing_heap_test): the base of a VirtualAlloc allocation committed read-write over its whole
size opens a heap of that size, 64 KiB aligned, CUSTOM / WRITE_BACK / L0, SHARED |
SHARED_CROSS_ADAPTER | ALLOW_SHADER_ATOMICS; an inner address, a partial or reserve-only commit
and a read-only range are E_INVALIDARG. The backing is the range itself, imported with
VK_EXT_external_memory_host, which the device and the test device enable when present.
CheckFeatureSupport(EXISTING_HEAPS) follows the extension. Placed resources in such a heap are
refused (E_NOTIMPL, logged) until the placed path addresses memory outside the arena.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
